Task Name: Dynamically Render Components in Task Card based on Metadata
Description: Modify backend and frontend to store and use task metadata (`metadataJson`) to dynamically render specified frontend components (`MaterialManagement.tsx`, `ModelSelector.tsx`) within the "Site Visit" task card.
Timestamps:
  - Created: 2025-05-09T20:06:00Z 
  - Updated: 2025-05-09T20:30:00Z
Status: Completed
Assigned to: cline
Assigned by: user

Sub-Tasks:
  1. Backend - Update Type Definitions:
     - `backend/src/types/projectTemplate.types.ts`: Added `metadataJson` to `TaskTemplate`. (Completed)
     - `backend/src/types/project.types.ts`: Added `metadataJson` to `TaskBase`. (Completed)
  2. Backend - Update Prisma Schema:
     - `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`: Added `metadataJson` to `Task` model. (Completed)
     - Generated and applied migration `20250509143149_add_metadata_to_task`. (Completed)
  3. Backend - Update Task Template Constant:
     - `backend/src/constants/projectTaskTemplate.ts`: Added `metadataJson` with component paths to "Site Visit" task. (Completed)
     - Added a subtask named "BIM engineer to upload site measurements" to the "Site Visit" task for redundant component rendering. (Completed)
  4. Backend - Update DTOs:
     - `backend/src/dtos/project.dto.ts`: Added `metadataJson` to `CreateTaskDto` and `TaskResponseDto`. (Completed)
     - Added `metadataJson` to `UpdateTaskDto` for task updates. (Completed)
  5. Backend - Update Services and Repositories:
     - `backend/src/services/project/task.service.ts`: Ensured `metadataJson` is handled in `createTaskFromTemplate` and `transformToResponseDto`. (Completed)
     - `backend/src/repositories/task.repository.ts`: Fixed `create` and `update` methods to properly save `metadataJson` to the database. (Completed)
  6. Frontend - Update Type Definitions:
     - `frontend/src/hooks/useProject.ts`: Added `metadataJson` to `Task` interface. (Completed)
  7. Frontend - Update Task Card Component:
     - `frontend/src/components/dashboard/CollapsibleTaskCard.tsx`:
       - Added logic to parse `task.metadataJson`.
       - Conditionally render `MaterialManagement` and `ModelSelector` components (using `React.lazy` and `Suspense`) if "Site Visit" task and `frontendComponents` metadata are present.
       - Corrected import paths for lazy-loaded components.
       - Corrected `task.taskName` to `task.name`.
       - Added null checks for `project` prop when passing to child components. (Completed)
  8. Documentation - Update MBK Files:
     - `backend/src/constants/projectTaskTemplate.mbk`: Documented the addition of `metadataJson` and the new subtask. (Completed)
     - `backend/src/dtos/project.dto.mbk`: Created and documented the DTO changes. (Completed)
     - `backend/src/services/project/task.service.mbk`: Updated to reflect handling of `metadataJson`. (Completed)
     - `frontend/src/components/dashboard/CollapsibleTaskCard.mbk`: Created and documented the component changes. (Completed)
     - `frontend/src/hooks/useProject.mbk`: Created and documented the type changes. (Completed)

Implementation Details:
  - The components are now rendered in two ways for redundancy:
    1. Through the task's `metadataJson` when `task.name === "Site Visit"`.
    2. Through a specific subtask when `subtask.name === "BIM engineer to upload site measurements"`.
  - This ensures the components will be visible regardless of which condition is triggered first.
  - Fixed a critical issue in `TaskRepository.create` and `TaskRepository.update` methods that were not properly saving `metadataJson` to the database.

Next Steps:
  - User to test by creating a new project and verifying that the "Site Visit" task card shows both the `MaterialManagement` and `ModelSelector` components.
